  m_text: "What this shader reads: the camera's position and the depth behind it. For each pixel it measures how close the line of sight passes to the lamp and adds that much light, up to the first wall. It is a volume, not a flat picture: it stays round from every side.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>File: Packages \u203A Toolbox \u203A Shaders \u203A Light-And-Space \u203A Glow-Volume.shader</color></size>"
